<!-- generated by tmvp from config.yaml — do not edit; regenerate with: tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> skill sync -->
# reqsume (tmvp)

Always call tmvp as `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> …` — it can only reach reqsume.

## Envs
- `dev` (destructive allowed)
- `staging`
- `prod`

## Systems
- `db` — postgres — envs: dev, staging, prod
- `cluster` — k8s — envs: dev, staging, prod
- `admin` — web — envs: dev, staging, prod

## Rules
1. Reads batch across envs: `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> all <system> <verb> … --reason "<task>"` (`--diff` to compare).
2. Writes only via `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> write <env> <system> <verb> … --reason "<why>"` — one env, only when the user asked; `--preview` first where supported.
3. `login_required` → show the user the exact command tmvp names (they run it), then retry. Never log in for them.
4. Never print, ask for or handle secret values. config.yaml holds only `$(commands)`.
5. Reach reqsume systems only through tmvp, never raw ssh, psql, kubectl or curl to its hosts: tmvp enforces read-only, timeouts and the audit log. A container name may be a prefix (`docker logs app-web`).
6. Multi-step investigation (several reads, then compare or drill in) → one program: `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> code run <file.js|name> --json`. Check saved scripts first with `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> code scripts`, then import tmvp's modules before composing raw ops (`tmvp code modules`: `tmvp:drift` compare envs / odd one out / stray whitespace, `tmvp:evidence` gather reads per env / log hits / lagging envs, `tmvp:health` failing systems); save a reusable one as `scripts/<name>.js` (first `//` line = description, no secrets). API: `tmvp llms code-mode`.

## Learn the rest from tmvp
- `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> envs` · `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> systems [env]`
- `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> <env> <system> ls` — what exists (tables, collections, pages, apis, saved items)
- `tmvp verbs [type]` · `tmvp llms [topic]` · any command + `--llmhelp`
- Saved items live in `<asset root>/<system>/{queries,scripts,pages,apis}/` (asset roots, first match wins: `assets`); run one with `tmvp --skill <SKILLDIR> <env> <system> @name`.
